 ### [Pre-Integration Lookup](2854-pre-integration-lookup.md)
-Replaces iterative accumulation within a slab with a single texture fetch from a pre-computed table, solving shading inaccuracies from linear interpolation. Choose when high accuracy is needed per-slab without per-sample shading cost.
+Pre-integration lookup is a technique in direct volume ray casting that replaces the iterative accumulation of color and opacity within a volume slab with a single texture fetch from a pre-computed table. It solves the problem of shading and color inaccuracies caused by linear interpolation of scalar values across a slab, which violates the non-linear optical properties of light attenuation. It sets itself apart from standard ray casting by moving the integration step from the rendering loop to an offline or on-the-fly pre-computation phase, and from [Simplified Pre-integration](6186-simplified-pre-integration.md) by accounting for color attenuation within the slab rather than neglecting it. See [Pre-Integration Lookup](2854-pre-integration-lookup.md).
 
 ### [Binary Swap Compositing](3264-binary-swap-compositing.md)
-A parallel scheme for distributed-memory rendering that reduces network congestion by dividing communication over multiple rounds. Choose for massively parallel processing to keep all processors busy.
+Binary Swap Compositing is a parallel image compositing scheme for distributed-memory volume rendering that reduces network congestion by dividing communication between processors over multiple rounds. Unlike naive binary compositing where many processors become idle at the top of the tree, Binary Swap ensures every processor participates in all stages of the compositing process by splitting the image plane into two pieces and having each processor take responsibility for one piece during exchange and compositing. It is particularly suitable for massively parallel processing because it keeps all processors busy and decreases the image size for sending/compositing at each stage. See [Binary Swap Compositing](3264-binary-swap-compositing.md).
 
 ### [Screen-space Post-processing](3621-screen-space-post-processing.md)
